  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power Sector Support Program</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa Apoyo al Sector de Energa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Apoyar actividades en el sector elctrico que ayuden a promover el desarrollo sostenible del sector e institucionalicen polticas y programas para: (i) establecer planificacin y prioridades en el sector; (ii) mejorar un entorno que incentive la reduccin de prdidas y la eficiencia de manera sostenible; (iii) proveer fortalecimiento institucional para afianzar la capacidad reguladora en el sector; (iv) fortalecer la compaa proveedora del servicio pblico; (v) promover la conciencia social que apoye la reduccin de prdidas. Alcanzar estos objetivos ayudar a mejorar la estabilidad financiera de la compaa de servicios y del sector y a reducir las prdidas que impactan en el costo para todos los consumidores. Otro de los efectos deseados de un programa exitoso sera contribuir a un entorno mejorado para recibir nuevas inversiones, que por ende contribuya a la competitividad y crecimiento de Guyana.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support activities in the electricity sector that will help promote the sustainable development of the energy sector and institutionalize policies and programs to (i) establish planning and priority setting in the sector; (ii) improve the enabling environment to encourage sustainable energy loss reduction and efficiency; (iii) provide institutional strenghtening in order to assure regulatory capacity of the sector; (iv) strengthen the power utility provider (GPL) in order to address loss reduction on a sustainable basis, efficiency and quality of service; and (v) promote social awareness to curb loss reduction. Achieving these objectives will help to improve the financial stability of the company and the sector itself by bringing back &quot;lost&quot; customers, improving long term planning for the sector, and reducing losses that increase costs to all consumers. One of the desired effects of a successful program would also be an improved environment for new investment, thereby contributing to Guyana&apos;s competitiveness and growth.</narrative>
  </description>
